{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgSamnPRkKHbo8a9W6FS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RnqjwodxkrQhedeZfafAtY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > plan.md <<'EOF'\n# 1-Page Marketing Plan — Taller Lento\n\n*Lucía Ferreyra · ceramics studio · Chacarita, Buenos Aires · drafted 3 October 2026*\n\n> This draft comes from your brief. You weren't available, so where something was missing I made a best guess. Every guess is listed under **\"Assumptions I made\"** at the bottom. Change anything that doesn't feel right. This is your plan.\n\n## The foundation\n\n**The item:** Wheel-throwing classes at Taller Lento. That means the monthly group (Saturdays 10–13, max 6 people, ARS 120,000/month, clay and firing included) and the 2.5-hour taster \"Probá el torno\" (ARS 40,000). The mugs matter too, but mostly as the shop window that brings people into the studio.\n\n**The sale (what \"it worked\" means):** A stranger books a class (the monthly group, or a taster that turns into the monthly) and then **stays past their second month**. A tourist buying one mug is nice, but it doesn't count as a sale in this plan.\n\n**6-month target (by early April 2027):** Saturday group full (6/6) every month · a Wednesday 19–22 group running with 4+ students · more students staying past month 2.\n\n**Limits:** about 5 hours a week of marketing · about US$50 a month (ARS 70,000), not counting the fair stall.\n\n---\n\n## The grid\n\n| | | |\n|---|---|---|\n| **BEFORE**: strangers who don't know you yet | | |\n| **1. Target market** | **2. Message** | **3. Media** |\n| **DURING**: people who showed interest | | |\n| **4. Capture leads** | **5. Nurture leads** | **6. Sales conversion** |\n| **AFTER**: your students | | |\n| **7. World-class experience** | **8. Lifetime value** | **9. Referrals** |\n\n## BEFORE: strangers who don't know you yet\n\n### 1. Target market\n*In plain words: who exactly this is for. Not \"everyone\".*\n\n- **Main:** women aged 28–45 with office, design or tech jobs who live in Chacarita, Colegiales, Villa Crespo or Palermo. They're tired of screens and want a calm weekly ritual with their hands. They often come with a friend.\n- **The Wednesday group** is for the same women who can't give up their Saturday morning. For them it's an after-work plan.\n- **Second group:** English-speaking expats and digital nomads in the same barrios. You can teach the class in English.\n- **Not the target for classes:** tourists (they buy one mug and leave within a week) and cafés asking for wholesale. Say no kindly: the margins are bad and it eats kiln space.\n\n### 2. Message\n*In plain words: what you say to those people so they care.*\n\n- **Main line:** ES *\"3 horas por semana lejos de la pantalla, con las manos en el barro.\"* / EN *\"Three hours a week off-screen, hands in clay.\"*\n- **Proof that makes it real:** max 6 people · clay and firing included · you keep everything you make · 10 minutes' walk from Lacroze.\n- **At the fair, the hook is the mug in their hand:** *\"¿Te gusta? Te enseño a hacerla.\"* / *\"Like it? I'll teach you to make it.\"*\n- **The first step is small and low-risk:** the taster \"Probá el torno\".\n- Write every post and caption in **Spanish and English**.\n\n### 3. Media\n*In plain words: where you'll reach those people. Go where they already are, not just where it's easy to post.*\n\n- **The Sunday fair** is your best room: people are already touching your work and asking \"do you give classes?\"\n- **Instagram:** 2 Reels of the wheel a week (they get 5–10x the views of photos), with bilingual captions and local hashtags (#Chacarita #ceramica #clasesdeceramica).\n- **Google Maps:** a free listing, \"Taller Lento – clases de cerámica\". People search \"clases de cerámica cerca de mí\", and right now you don't show up.\n- **Expat groups:** one post a month in Buenos Aires expat groups (Facebook or WhatsApp) about the class in English.\n- **About US$25/month:** boost your best Reel to women aged 25–45 in your 4 barrios.\n\n## DURING: people who showed interest\n\n### 4. Capture leads\n*In plain words: a \"lead\" is someone who showed interest **and gave you a way to contact them** (here, their WhatsApp). Today \"follow me on Instagram\" is where it ends. This square fixes that.*\n\n- **At the fair:** a small sign and cards with a **QR code that opens WhatsApp with a ready-written message** (\"Hola! Quiero info de clases\"). Make it free with a `wa.me` link and any free QR generator. Also keep a notebook on the table: *\"Avisame del próximo taller de prueba\"* (name + WhatsApp).\n- **Instagram bio:** replace the PDF price list with the same WhatsApp link plus \"Próximo taller de prueba / Next taster: [date]\".\n- **Switch to WhatsApp Business** (free, same number). Use labels to sort people: *Interesada · Taster · Alumna · Ex-alumna*.\n- **One Google Sheet called \"Leads\"** with columns: name · WhatsApp · where they came from (fair / IG / Maps / friend) · date · status.\n\n### 5. Nurture leads\n*In plain words: stay in touch, gently, so they trust you before you ask them to book.*\n\n- **Within 48 hours of each fair,** message everyone from the notebook and QR with a short Reel and the next taster date.\n- **Every 2 weeks, one WhatsApp broadcast:** a kiln photo, seats left, the next taster. (Broadcasts only reach people who saved your number, so ask them to save it.) Don't send more often than that.\n- **Instagram stories:** students' pieces (ask permission first), kiln openings, \"a Saturday at the taller\".\n- Expats get the English version of every message.\n\n### 6. Sales conversion\n*In plain words: how an interested person becomes a booked student who stays.*\n\n- **A fixed taster date every month** (e.g. last Saturday of the month, 15:00). A date is much easier to sell than \"when enough people ask\".\n- **Use the kiln as your follow-up.** Taster pieces are fired later, so you always have a reason to write back: *\"¡Tu taza salió del horno! There's a seat on Saturday / Wednesday.\"* Picking up the piece is also the moment to offer the monthly class face to face.\n- **Taster-to-monthly credit:** join the monthly within 7 days and get ARS 20,000 off the first month.\n- **Friends together:** 2 friends who sign up together get 10% off each.\n- **Wednesday group:** start collecting a \"Wednesday list\" now. The group opens as soon as **4 people pay the first month** (Mercado Pago link).\n\n## AFTER: your students\n\n### 7. World-class experience\n*In plain words: deliver so well that students become fans.*\n\n- **A welcome WhatsApp the day before the first class:** address, how to walk from Lacroze, what to wear, aprons provided. Save it as a quick reply in WhatsApp Business so it's one tap.\n- **Everyone leaves the first class having thrown something,** and you send each person a photo of their first piece.\n- **Give each month a goal:** week 1 centering → week 2 cylinders → week 3 mugs and bowls → week 4 trimming and glazing (yes, they can use the yerba green).\n- **Small rituals:** a mate break every class, and kiln opening as a small celebration.\n- **Missed a class?** Message the same day: *\"We missed you, here's what we did.\"* People who drift away usually start by missing one class.\n\n### 8. Lifetime value\n*In plain words: keep each student longer and let them spend more if they want to. Your brief says the 3+ month students are your best people, so this is the most important square.*\n\n- **Make-up classes:** miss a Saturday, come on Wednesday (and the other way round). This answers \"my schedule changed\", the #1 reason students leave.\n- **Renewal message 1 week before the month ends:** *\"Your seat is saved until [date]\"* plus what they'll make next month.\n- **Projects for months 2–3:** a set of 4 matching mugs, a serving bowl, their own glaze test. Give people a reason to stay.\n- **3-month pack:** ARS 330,000 paid up front (instead of 360,000).\n- **Students get 15% off mugs.** They already buy them as gifts.\n- **Taster gift vouchers:** sell them at the fair to local gift buyers. **Día de la Madre is Sunday 18 October**, and Christmas comes after that.\n- **Every ~3 months, message ex-students:** *\"A seat opened on Wednesday.\"*\n\n### 9. Referrals\n*In plain words: deliberately get happy students to bring others. Most of your students already came this way, so make it a habit instead of luck.*\n\n- **\"Traé una amiga\":** when a friend you bring signs up for a month, you get a mug of your choice. It costs you clay and kiln space, but it's worth ARS 28,000 to them.\n- **Ask at happy moments:** kiln opening, end of month 3.\n- **Make it easy:** a ready-to-forward WhatsApp message with the QR and the next taster date.\n- **Ask happy students for a Google Maps review,** and to tag @taller.lento when they post their pieces.\n\n---\n\n## How this fits in 5 hours a week\n\n| When | What | Time |\n|---|---|---|\n| During class/throwing | Film 3–4 short clips on your phone (hands, wheel, kiln) | 0 extra |\n| Monday | Message last Sunday's fair leads · update the Leads sheet | 1 h |\n| Tuesday | Edit + post Reel #1 (bilingual caption) | 1 h |\n| Thursday | Edit + post Reel #2 · stories | 1 h |\n| Friday | Taster / renewal / missed-class follow-ups on WhatsApp | 1 h |\n| Every other week | WhatsApp broadcast · monthly expat-group post | 1 h |\n\n## Where the US$50 (≈ ARS 70,000) a month goes\n\n| Item | Per month |\n|---|---|\n| Instagram boost of your best Reel (4 barrios, women 25–45) | ≈ ARS 35,000 |\n| Printed QR cards + small fair sign (first month; later months this money goes to boosts) | ≈ ARS 20,000 |\n| Reserve: referral mugs, mate/snacks for tasters | ≈ ARS 15,000 |\n| WhatsApp Business, Google Maps, Google Sheets, QR codes | free |\n\n## First 30 days (October 2026)\n\n1. Switch to WhatsApp Business. Set up the labels and quick replies (welcome, prices, next taster).\n2. Make the `wa.me` link and the QR code. Print the cards and sign. Update the Instagram bio.\n3. Create the Google Maps listing (Google Business Profile) and ask 3 current students for a review.\n4. Set a fixed taster date for the rest of the year and announce it.\n5. Make taster gift vouchers for **Día de la Madre (18 Oct)** and sell them at the fair.\n6. Start the \"Wednesday list\" with current students' friends and fair leads.\n\n## Numbers to check once a month (add them to the Leads sheet)\n\n- Seats filled: Saturday __/6 · Wednesday __/6\n- New leads this month (and where from)\n- Tasters booked → how many joined the monthly\n- Students who stayed past month 2 · students at 3+ months\n- Referrals (new students who came through a student)\n\n## Things deliberately left out\n\nWholesale to cafés, international shipping, a website and an email list. They would cost time you don't have and wouldn't move the 6-month goal. WhatsApp + Instagram + Google Maps + one Sheet is enough.\n\n## Assumptions I made (please check)\n\n1. **The sale = a booked class that sticks,** not mug sales. Taken from your \"when I picture it worked…\" paragraph.\n2. **The prices for the new offers are my suggestions:** ARS 20,000 taster credit, 10% off for friends signing up together, ARS 330,000 3-month pack, 15% off mugs for students, a free mug per referral. Adjust them to your margins.\n3. **The Wednesday group** opens once 4 people have paid, not on a fixed date. Buenos Aires empties in January, so if it hasn't filled by December, aim for a start in early March when routines restart.\n4. **Make-up classes between groups** only work once the Wednesday group exists. Until then, offer a make-up seat in the monthly taster.\n5. **The monthly taster** is fixed to the last Saturday afternoon of the month. Pick another slot if that one clashes.\n6. **Exchange rate:** about ARS 1,400 = US$1, based on your own figures (US$50 ≈ ARS 70,000).\n\n---\n\n*This is a living document. Look at it again every 3 months and change one square at a time instead of rewriting the whole plan.*\n\n### How to put plan.csv into Google Sheets\nGoogle Sheets → **File → Import → Upload** → choose `plan.csv` → **Replace current sheet**. Then, to make it readable: make columns A–C wide (~390 px), select rows 6, 8 and 10 and set **Wrap** + **Top align** + a tall row height (~260 px). Colour the BEFORE / DURING / AFTER rows (5, 7, 9) in three soft colours, and freeze rows 1–3.\nEOF\nls -la"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2753,"cache_read_input_tokens":28934,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2753},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eaa9753d-c7d3-48e6-b3c6-f635b154a54b","uuid":"1bbc40af-7bff-4804-a141-057694d1bb50","timestamp":"2026-10-04T02:54:46.815Z","request_id":"req_011CfgSam1FxbM5Q6sKVTtPR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RnqjwodxkrQhedeZfafAtY":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/mp-2GD9rL && cat > plan.md <<'EOF'\n# 1-Page Marketing Plan — Taller Lento\n\n*Lucía Ferreyra · ceramics studio · Chacarita, Buenos Aires · drafted 3 October 2026*\n\n> This draft comes from your brief. You weren't available, so where something was missing I made a best guess. Every guess is listed under **\"Assumptions I made\"** at the bottom. Change anything that doesn't feel right. This is your plan.\n\n## The foundation\n\n**The item:** Wheel-throwing classes at Taller Lento. That means the monthly group (Saturdays 10–13, max 6 people, ARS 120,000/month, clay and firing included) and the 2.5-hour taster \"Probá el torno\" (ARS 40,000). The mugs matter too, but mostly as the shop window that brings people into the studio.\n\n**The sale (what \"it worked\" means):** A stranger books a class (the monthly group, or a taster that turns into the monthly) and then **stays past their second month**. A tourist buying one mug is nice, but it doesn't count as a sale in this plan.\n\n**6-month target (by early April 2027):** Saturday group full (6/6) every month · a Wednesday 19–22 group running with 4+ students · more students staying past month 2.\n\n**Limits:** about 5 hours a week of marketing · about US$50 a month (ARS 70,000), not counting the fair stall.\n\n---\n\n## The grid\n\n| | | |\n|---|---|---|\n| **BEFORE**: strangers who don't know you yet | | |\n| **1. Target market** | **2. Message** | **3. Media** |\n| **DURING**: people who showed interest | | |\n| **4. Capture leads** | **5. Nurture leads** | **6. Sales conversion** |\n| **AFTER**: your students | | |\n| **7. World-class experience** | **8. Lifetime value** | **9. Referrals** |\n\n## BEFORE: strangers who don't know you yet\n\n### 1. Target market\n*In plain words: who exactly this is for. Not \"everyone\".*\n\n- **Main:** women aged 28–45 with office, design or tech jobs who live in Chacarita, Colegiales, Villa Crespo or Palermo. They're tired of screens and want a calm weekly ritual with their hands. They often come with a friend.\n- **The Wednesday group** is for the same women who can't give up their Saturday morning. For them it's an after-work plan.\n- **Second group:** English-speaking expats and digital nomads in the same barrios. You can teach the class in English.\n- **Not the target for classes:** tourists (they buy one mug and leave within a week) and cafés asking for wholesale. Say no kindly: the margins are bad and it eats kiln space.\n\n### 2. Message\n*In plain words: what you say to those people so they care.*\n\n- **Main line:** ES *\"3 horas por semana lejos de la pantalla, con las manos en el barro.\"* / EN *\"Three hours a week off-screen, hands in clay.\"*\n- **Proof that makes it real:** max 6 people · clay and firing included · you keep everything you make · 10 minutes' walk from Lacroze.\n- **At the fair, the hook is the mug in their hand:** *\"¿Te gusta? Te enseño a hacerla.\"* / *\"Like it? I'll teach you to make it.\"*\n- **The first step is small and low-risk:** the taster \"Probá el torno\".\n- Write every post and caption in **Spanish and English**.\n\n### 3. Media\n*In plain words: where you'll reach those people. Go where they already are, not just where it's easy to post.*\n\n- **The Sunday fair** is your best room: people are already touching your work and asking \"do you give classes?\"\n- **Instagram:** 2 Reels of the wheel a week (they get 5–10x the views of photos), with bilingual captions and local hashtags (#Chacarita #ceramica #clasesdeceramica).\n- **Google Maps:** a free listing, \"Taller Lento – clases de cerámica\". People search \"clases de cerámica cerca de mí\", and right now you don't show up.\n- **Expat groups:** one post a month in Buenos Aires expat groups (Facebook or WhatsApp) about the class in English.\n- **About US$25/month:** boost your best Reel to women aged 25–45 in your 4 barrios.\n\n## DURING: people who showed interest\n\n### 4. Capture leads\n*In plain words: a \"lead\" is someone who showed interest **and gave you a way to contact them** (here, their WhatsApp). Today \"follow me on Instagram\" is where it ends. This square fixes that.*\n\n- **At the fair:** a small sign and cards with a **QR code that opens WhatsApp with a ready-written message** (\"Hola! Quiero info de clases\"). Make it free with a `wa.me` link and any free QR generator. Also keep a notebook on the table: *\"Avisame del próximo taller de prueba\"* (name + WhatsApp).\n- **Instagram bio:** replace the PDF price list with the same WhatsApp link plus \"Próximo taller de prueba / Next taster: [date]\".\n- **Switch to WhatsApp Business** (free, same number). Use labels to sort people: *Interesada · Taster · Alumna · Ex-alumna*.\n- **One Google Sheet called \"Leads\"** with columns: name · WhatsApp · where they came from (fair / IG / Maps / friend) · date · status.\n\n### 5. Nurture leads\n*In plain words: stay in touch, gently, so they trust you before you ask them to book.*\n\n- **Within 48 hours of each fair,** message everyone from the notebook and QR with a short Reel and the next taster date.\n- **Every 2 weeks, one WhatsApp broadcast:** a kiln photo, seats left, the next taster. (Broadcasts only reach people who saved your number, so ask them to save it.) Don't send more often than that.\n- **Instagram stories:** students' pieces (ask permission first), kiln openings, \"a Saturday at the taller\".\n- Expats get the English version of every message.\n\n### 6. Sales conversion\n*In plain words: how an interested person becomes a booked student who stays.*\n\n- **A fixed taster date every month** (e.g. last Saturday of the month, 15:00). A date is much easier to sell than \"when enough people ask\".\n- **Use the kiln as your follow-up.** Taster pieces are fired later, so you always have a reason to write back: *\"¡Tu taza salió del horno! There's a seat on Saturday / Wednesday.\"* Picking up the piece is also the moment to offer the monthly class face to face.\n- **Taster-to-monthly credit:** join the monthly within 7 days and get ARS 20,000 off the first month.\n- **Friends together:** 2 friends who sign up together get 10% off each.\n- **Wednesday group:** start collecting a \"Wednesday list\" now. The group opens as soon as **4 people pay the first month** (Mercado Pago link).\n\n## AFTER: your students\n\n### 7. World-class experience\n*In plain words: deliver so well that students become fans.*\n\n- **A welcome WhatsApp the day before the first class:** address, how to walk from Lacroze, what to wear, aprons provided. Save it as a quick reply in WhatsApp Business so it's one tap.\n- **Everyone leaves the first class having thrown something,** and you send each person a photo of their first piece.\n- **Give each month a goal:** week 1 centering → week 2 cylinders → week 3 mugs and bowls → week 4 trimming and glazing (yes, they can use the yerba green).\n- **Small rituals:** a mate break every class, and kiln opening as a small celebration.\n- **Missed a class?** Message the same day: *\"We missed you, here's what we did.\"* People who drift away usually start by missing one class.\n\n### 8. Lifetime value\n*In plain words: keep each student longer and let them spend more if they want to. Your brief says the 3+ month students are your best people, so this is the most important square.*\n\n- **Make-up classes:** miss a Saturday, come on Wednesday (and the other way round). This answers \"my schedule changed\", the #1 reason students leave.\n- **Renewal message 1 week before the month ends:** *\"Your seat is saved until [date]\"* plus what they'll make next month.\n- **Projects for months 2–3:** a set of 4 matching mugs, a serving bowl, their own glaze test. Give people a reason to stay.\n- **3-month pack:** ARS 330,000 paid up front (instead of 360,000).\n- **Students get 15% off mugs.** They already buy them as gifts.\n- **Taster gift vouchers:** sell them at the fair to local gift buyers. **Día de la Madre is Sunday 18 October**, and Christmas comes after that.\n- **Every ~3 months, message ex-students:** *\"A seat opened on Wednesday.\"*\n\n### 9. Referrals\n*In plain words: deliberately get happy students to bring others. Most of your students already came this way, so make it a habit instead of luck.*\n\n- **\"Traé una amiga\":** when a friend you bring signs up for a month, you get a mug of your choice. It costs you clay and kiln space, but it's worth ARS 28,000 to them.\n- **Ask at happy moments:** kiln opening, end of month 3.\n- **Make it easy:** a ready-to-forward WhatsApp message with the QR and the next taster date.\n- **Ask happy students for a Google Maps review,** and to tag @taller.lento when they post their pieces.\n\n---\n\n## How this fits in 5 hours a week\n\n| When | What | Time |\n|---|---|---|\n| During class/throwing | Film 3–4 short clips on your phone (hands, wheel, kiln) | 0 extra |\n| Monday | Message last Sunday's fair leads · update the Leads sheet | 1 h |\n| Tuesday | Edit + post Reel #1 (bilingual caption) | 1 h |\n| Thursday | Edit + post Reel #2 · stories | 1 h |\n| Friday | Taster / renewal / missed-class follow-ups on WhatsApp | 1 h |\n| Every other week | WhatsApp broadcast · monthly expat-group post | 1 h |\n\n## Where the US$50 (≈ ARS 70,000) a month goes\n\n| Item | Per month |\n|---|---|\n| Instagram boost of your best Reel (4 barrios, women 25–45) | ≈ ARS 35,000 |\n| Printed QR cards + small fair sign (first month; later months this money goes to boosts) | ≈ ARS 20,000 |\n| Reserve: referral mugs, mate/snacks for tasters | ≈ ARS 15,000 |\n| WhatsApp Business, Google Maps, Google Sheets, QR codes | free |\n\n## First 30 days (October 2026)\n\n1. Switch to WhatsApp Business. Set up the labels and quick replies (welcome, prices, next taster).\n2. Make the `wa.me` link and the QR code. Print the cards and sign. Update the Instagram bio.\n3. Create the Google Maps listing (Google Business Profile) and ask 3 current students for a review.\n4. Set a fixed taster date for the rest of the year and announce it.\n5. Make taster gift vouchers for **Día de la Madre (18 Oct)** and sell them at the fair.\n6. Start the \"Wednesday list\" with current students' friends and fair leads.\n\n## Numbers to check once a month (add them to the Leads sheet)\n\n- Seats filled: Saturday __/6 · Wednesday __/6\n- New leads this month (and where from)\n- Tasters booked → how many joined the monthly\n- Students who stayed past month 2 · students at 3+ months\n- Referrals (new students who came through a student)\n\n## Things deliberately left out\n\nWholesale to cafés, international shipping, a website and an email list. They would cost time you don't have and wouldn't move the 6-month goal. WhatsApp + Instagram + Google Maps + one Sheet is enough.\n\n## Assumptions I made (please check)\n\n1. **The sale = a booked class that sticks,** not mug sales. Taken from your \"when I picture it worked…\" paragraph.\n2. **The prices for the new offers are my suggestions:** ARS 20,000 taster credit, 10% off for friends signing up together, ARS 330,000 3-month pack, 15% off mugs for students, a free mug per referral. Adjust them to your margins.\n3. **The Wednesday group** opens once 4 people have paid, not on a fixed date. Buenos Aires empties in January, so if it hasn't filled by December, aim for a start in early March when routines restart.\n4. **Make-up classes between groups** only work once the Wednesday group exists. Until then, offer a make-up seat in the monthly taster.\n5. **The monthly taster** is fixed to the last Saturday afternoon of the month. Pick another slot if that one clashes.\n6. **Exchange rate:** about ARS 1,400 = US$1, based on your own figures (US$50 ≈ ARS 70,000).\n\n---\n\n*This is a living document. Look at it again every 3 months and change one square at a time instead of rewriting the whole plan.*\n\n### How to put plan.csv into Google Sheets\nGoogle Sheets → **File → Import → Upload** → choose `plan.csv` → **Replace current sheet**. Then, to make it readable: make columns A–C wide (~390 px), select rows 6, 8 and 10 and set **Wrap** + **Top align** + a tall row height (~260 px). Colour the BEFORE / DURING / AFTER rows (5, 7, 9) in three soft colours, and freeze rows 1–3.\nEOF\nls -la"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01RnqjwodxkrQhedeZfafAtY":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/mp-2GD9rL"}}}
