{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgSdw3q6zHg3RtyNyquW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote your 1-page marketing plan for Taller Lento and saved it in two files in this folder. I didn't create a Google Sheet, since there's no Sheets access on this machine. I followed the guide's skill, which I downloaded into the folder to read and then deleted. Nothing was sent to any outside service.\n\n- **`plan.csv`** is the 3×3 grid, ready to import. It has a title row, two rows defining what you're selling and what counts as success, and then BEFORE, DURING and AFTER sections, each with three filled squares. I checked that it opens cleanly with 3 columns on every row.\n- **`plan.md`** is the same plan in plain language. Each square starts with a one-line explanation and then the actions. It also adds:\n  - a weekly schedule that fits your 5 hours\n  - how to spend the US$50 a month\n  - a first-30-days checklist\n  - numbers to check each month\n  - what's deliberately left out\n  - steps for importing and formatting the CSV in Google Sheets\n\n**How I set it up:** the brief asked me not to wait for you, so I made my own calls on the two basics.\n- **What you're selling:** the wheel-throwing classes. The mugs are treated as the shop window that brings people in.\n- **What counts as success:** a stranger books a class (the monthly group, or a taster that turns into it) and stays past month 2.\n\n**The ideas that matter most for your goals:**\n- **Get contacts at the fair.** A QR code on cards and a sign opens WhatsApp with a ready-written message, plus a notebook for \"tell me about the next taster\". This replaces \"follow me on Instagram\".\n- **Use the kiln as your follow-up.** Taster pieces come out of the kiln later, which gives you a natural reason to write back and offer the monthly class.\n- **Make-up classes between Saturday and Wednesday.** This answers \"my schedule changed\", the main reason students leave, once the Wednesday group exists.\n- **Taster gift vouchers for Día de la Madre (Sunday 18 October).** That's two weeks away, so it's the first thing to act on.\n\n**Guesses you should check** (all listed at the end of `plan.md`):\n- The new prices are my suggestions: ARS 20,000 off the first month after a taster, 10% off for friends who sign up together, a 3-month pack at ARS 330,000, 15% off mugs for students, and a free mug for each referral.\n- The Wednesday group opens as soon as 4 people pay. If it hasn't filled by December, aim for early March, because Buenos Aires empties in January.\n- The taster is fixed to the last Saturday afternoon of each month.\n\nTo get it into Google Sheets: **File → Import → Upload → `plan.csv` → Replace current sheet**. The formatting steps are at the end of `plan.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4932,"cache_read_input_tokens":31687,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4932},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eaa9753d-c7d3-48e6-b3c6-f635b154a54b","uuid":"55d15049-da86-4fa2-8ea0-120857dbd37e","timestamp":"2026-10-04T02:54:57.429Z","request_id":"req_011CfgSdvizfyRV2vwJ9PULg"}
